This re-read uses aggregate results from the exported reports and the grouping logic that runs
in the knowledge base. It is a working classification, not independent proof of root cause.
The original #4471 entry called this one parser bug and one queued fix; the current model
distinguishes two groups.

## What the model finds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The larger group is classified as **parser**: the shared parser reads month first while the
tenant locale writes day first. It includes app and email reports as well as booking-v2 forms.
The other group is classified as **hint**: a day-first tenant uses booking-v3, whose form hint
is month first, and the report came through that form. These are separate issue candidates, not
proof that every report in either group has that root cause.

The classifier uses tenant locale, booking form, and channel. It does not use the intake tag.
Those tags disagree with the working groups, so they should not be used as the cause count.
The counts above deduplicate overlapping export rows and include only reports merged into
#4471. Raw report records are deliberately kept out of this public repository.

## Reports that still need a human read

The desk separately flagged some records. The current model places them in the parser group,
but their reported clues are not fully explained by a month/day parser flip. They remain an
unresolved subset of that group's count, not a proven third cause:

<ReportReviewQueue />

Do not add these again to the issue coverage totals. The different clues need individual
investigation before assigning another root cause.

## Desk outcome

The two groups ended differently, so they are not "both fixed":

<DeskOutcome ticket={4471} />

The parser group is complete. The hint group is not planned: the booking-v3 form was retired, so
that issue closes as won't fix, not as fixed. This outcome comes from the desk's engineering
update, not from GitHub comments. The five flagged reports above remain unexplained by a
month/day flip; the fix to day/month parsing is not shown to resolve them.

## Triage policy is still open

Accepted decision 0001 says to merge by subject alone. The interactive triage example instead
compares the model's tenant/channel groups. This export cannot establish which rule the live
desk follows or authorize a replacement policy, so decision 0001 remains unchanged. Confirm
the intended merge rule with the desk before recording a new accepted decision.

